    {
      "fileName": "dual-form-weapon.json",
      "id": "XWtNGOkMHcrdrRw8",
      "name": "Dual-Form Weapon",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "XWtNGOkMHcrdrRw8",
        "folder": "xbCKkmp7Z0yDZjMH",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Dual-Form Weapon",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "passive"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>Your innovation has replaceable interlocking pieces that you can use to transform it into another type of weapon. When you select this feat, choose a level 0 weapon. It must be either a common weapon or another to which you have access. This weapon becomes your innovation's second configuration.</p>\n<p>Select a new set of weapon modifications for this new configuration. You can spend two Interact actions to switch your weapon innovation between the two configurations. These actions don't need to be taken consecutively, but if you've provided the first and not the second, the weapon is non-functional as it is stranded between states. Your weapon's Bulk is always the greater Bulk of the two configurations, regardless of which configuration it's in—if one weapon is smaller than the other, you still need to keep any weapon parts on hand. Any runes on your weapon innovation affect the second weapon configuration as long as it would normally qualify for them.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 4
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": [
              {
                "value": "expert overdrive"
              },
              {
                "value": "weapon innovation"
              }
            ]
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder Guns & Gears"
          },
          "rules": [],
          "traits": {
            "rarity": "common",
            "value": [
              "inventor",
              "modification"
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "feat"
      },
      "level": 4,
      "category": "class"
    },
    {
      "fileName": "duo-dragon-kick.json",
      "id": "wOb5YGq1EcRn3lwl",
      "name": "Duo Dragon Kick",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "wOb5YGq1EcRn3lwl",
        "folder": "xbCKkmp7Z0yDZjMH",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Duo Dragon Kick",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "action"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": 2
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p><strong>Requirements</strong> Your construct innovation is adjacent to you.</p><hr /><p>You've practiced an impressive spin technique with your construct, automatically attacking in tandem as you launch each other through the air. You Command your construct companion to fight alongside you, after which you both @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Leap] in the same direction, making an unarmed Strike at the start or end of the Leap; this uses your companion's actions for the turn. If the Strikes both hit the same creature, combine their damage for the purposes of resistances and weaknesses.</p>\n<p><strong>Unstable Function</strong> You spin farther and higher, though the extreme movement risks discombobulating your innovation. Add the unstable trait to Duo Dragon Kick. Increase the distance of your Leaps by 10 feet if horizontal or 5 feet if vertical.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 4
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": [
              {
                "value": "construct innovation"
              }
            ]
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder Lost Omens Tian Xia Character Guide"
          },
          "rules": [
            {
              "key": "RollOption",
              "label": "PF2E.SpecificRule.Inventor.Unstable.UnstableFunction.Label",
              "option": "unstable-state",
              "toggleable": true
            },
            {
              "itemId": "{item|id}",
              "key": "ItemAlteration",
              "mode": "add",
              "predicate": [
